+++
title = "Installation"
template = "docs"
+++

Revela runs on **Windows**, **macOS**, and **Linux**. Choose the installation method that suits you best.

## Option 1: Standalone (Recommended)

Download, extract, run. No prerequisites needed.

### Windows (x64)

```bash
# Download and extract
curl -L https://github.com/Spectara/Revela/releases/latest/download/revela-win-x64-standalone.zip -o revela.zip
Expand-Archive revela.zip -DestinationPath D:\Revela
```

Or simply download the `.zip` from [GitHub Releases](https://github.com/Spectara/Revela/releases), right-click → Extract All.

### macOS (Apple Silicon)

```bash
curl -L https://github.com/Spectara/Revela/releases/latest/download/revela-osx-arm64-standalone.tar.gz | tar xz
chmod +x revela
```

### Linux (x64)

```bash
curl -L https://github.com/Spectara/Revela/releases/latest/download/revela-linux-x64-standalone.tar.gz | tar xz
chmod +x revela
```

### Standalone Directory Structure

After extraction, your directory looks like this:

```
D:\Revela\
├── revela.exe          # The executable
├── revela.json         # Global configuration (created on first run)
└── projects/           # Your projects (one folder per site)
    └── MyPhotos/
        ├── project.json
        ├── site.json
        ├── source/
        └── output/
```

**Key feature:** In standalone mode, Revela manages multiple projects in the `projects/` folder. Double-click `revela.exe` to start the interactive menu with project selection.

---

## Option 2: .NET Global Tool

If you have the [.NET SDK](https://dotnet.microsoft.com/download) installed (version 10 or later), you can install Revela as a global tool.

> **Not on NuGet.org yet:** Revela packages are not published on NuGet.org, so `dotnet tool install -g Spectara.Revela` on its own will fail. Every package is attached to each [GitHub Release](https://github.com/Spectara/Revela/releases) instead.

1. Download `Spectara.Revela.<version>.nupkg` from the release into a folder, for example `./revela-packages`. Download the plugin and theme `.nupkg` files you want into the same folder (at least `Spectara.Revela.Themes.Lumina.<version>.nupkg`).
2. Install the tool from that folder:

   ```bash
   dotnet tool install -g Spectara.Revela --version <version> --add-source ./revela-packages
   ```

3. Tell Revela where to find plugins and themes (the tool has no bundled packages):

   ```bash
   revela config feed add releases /absolute/path/to/revela-packages
   ```

   This adds the folder to `dependencies.feeds` in your global `revela.json`, so it is trusted for every project.

### Update

Download the new `.nupkg` files into the same folder, then:

```bash
dotnet tool update -g Spectara.Revela --version <version> --add-source ./revela-packages
```

### Usage

Navigate to your project directory and run commands directly:

```bash
cd ~/my-photography-website
revela generate all
```

### Differences from Standalone

| Feature | Standalone | .NET Global Tool |
|---------|-----------|-----------------|
| **Prerequisites** | None | .NET 10 SDK |
| **Projects** | Multiple (managed in `projects/`) | One per directory |
| **Config location** | Next to `revela.exe` | `%APPDATA%/Revela/` |
| **Project selection** | Interactive menu | Navigate to project dir |
| **`revela projects`** | Available | Not available |
| **Interactive mode** | Double-click exe | Run `revela` without args |

---

## First Run

After installation, run `revela` without arguments:

```bash
revela
```

On first run, the **Setup Wizard** starts automatically:

1. **Install themes and plugins**: full or custom installation
2. **Create a project**: folder name and settings
3. **Ready to go**: add photos and generate

See the [User Journey](../user-journey/) for a complete walkthrough.

---

## Verifying Installation

```bash
revela --version
```

Check where Revela stores its configuration:

```bash
revela config locations
```

---

## Updating

### Standalone

Download the latest release and replace `revela.exe`. Your `revela.json` and `projects/` folder are preserved. Themes and plugins are built into the Standalone executable, so they update with it.

### .NET Global Tool

Download the new release's `.nupkg` files into your package folder, then:

```bash
dotnet tool update -g Spectara.Revela --version <version> --add-source ./revela-packages
```

After updating, restore your dependencies:

```bash
revela restore
```

---

## Troubleshooting

### `revela: command not found`

Revela isn't on your `PATH`.

- **Windows**: add the folder containing `revela.exe` to your `Path` environment variable.
- **macOS / Linux**: create a symlink (`sudo ln -s /path/to/revela /usr/local/bin/revela`) or add the folder to your `PATH`.

### `Permission denied` (macOS / Linux)

The binary isn't executable yet:

```bash
chmod +x /path/to/revela
```

### Windows SmartScreen warning

The executable isn't code-signed yet. Click **More info → Run anyway**.

### macOS "cannot be opened because the developer cannot be verified"

Allow it once under **System Settings → Privacy & Security → Open Anyway**, or clear the quarantine flag from the terminal:

```bash
xattr -d com.apple.quarantine /path/to/revela
```
